00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.240
Thought it might be a good idea to agree to some ground rules for the use of outer space

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.110
The Outer Space Treaty now agreed upon by over a hundred nations

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.179
Prohibits any country from placing nuclear weapons in outer space or on any celestial body it also

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:46.439
Explicitly forbids any nation from claiming a space resource such as the moon or a planet and so far. It's worked out to date

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.930
No government has attempted to claim a celestial body

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.210
But what if that were to change?

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.100
Let's say North Korean dictator

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.559
Kim jong-un got it into his head that he wanted to own the moon and somehow managed to launch a manned mission and

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:00.520
successfully land North Koreans on the moon

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:07.470
They plant the flag and a little statue of the glorious leader and hunker down to defend their new prize from all invaders now what?

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:08.650
realistically

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:14.969
Kim jong-un would likely get a stern talking-to by the other members of the treaty and suffer even more sanctions here on earth and the

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.930
incident would be forgotten if

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.930
However the North Koreans managed to construct some form of delivery system for nuclear warheads on the moon

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:25.139
The global response would probably be far more severe

00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:32.368
But what if an individual tried to claim a celestial body while the outer space treaty does say non government entities will require?

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.570
Authorization to operate in outer space and are the responsibility of their parent nation

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:40.320
It does not explicitly state that an individual cannot claim a planet or moon

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:47.339
With the recent success of the SpaceX Falcon Heavy rocket we need to consider the possibility that Elon Musk could go full

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.210
Supervillain and claim Mars as his own, but how would that work exactly?

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:59.459
What does it take to legally own something the size of Mars the doctrine of first possession basically the legal equivalent of Finders Keepers?

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:02.368
States that in order to claim something you must first show

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:06.899
Intention and control and possession goes into effect as soon as those two criteria are met

00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:13.469
Simply planting a spacex flag on the red planet is enough to show the intent of ownership, but how do you control the whole?

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.240
The easiest way would probably be to build simple roads and tiny outposts over much of the planet surface

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.740
Once a road is built

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:25.119
You could reasonably claim a certain amount of territory on either side of it enough roads

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.200
And you've secured the whole planet of course the idea of first possession is not

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.020
Universally agreed upon so this claim would be iffy at best

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:36.999
Back on earth American authorities would likely step in and demand the claim be redacted

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:42.790
If Ilan refused further actions would be taken if the members of the treaty considered his claim to be a threat to the earth

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:48.850
The only way to ensure complete ownership of Mars would be to do it all at once you'd have to send enough manpower

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.310
materials and supplies to establish a

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.459
self-sufficient colony and leave the earth behind entirely if

00:02:54.530 --> 00:03:00.339
you could do that the only way to get you to renounce your claim would be for other nations to physically come to Mars and

